  97:     """
  98:     Move the small colored sprite into the hollow frame by stretching its shape to the frame interior.
  99: 
 100:     Input structure:
 101:     - The background is the dominant color.
 102:     - There are exactly two foreground colors: one forms a complete rectangular
 103:       one-pixel-thick frame, and the other forms one 4-connected sprite outside it.
 104:     - The frame interior is initially background.
 105: 
 106:     Rule:
 107:     - Clear the original sprite from its outside location.
 108:     - Map the sprite bbox to the frame interior bbox, sending bbox extremes to
 109:       interior extremes.
 110:     - Draw straight horizontal or vertical segments between mapped positions of
 111:       adjacent sprite pixels, then fill any enclosed background region inside
 112:       those drawn segments.
 113: 
 114:     Key insight:
 115:     The outside sprite is a miniature line/fill diagram for the frame interior,
 116:     not a bitmap to scale by block replication.
 117:     """
 118:     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
 119:     bg = get_bg(g)
 120:     colors = colors_present(g, exclude={bg})
 121:     assert len(colors) == 2, "expected one frame color and one sprite color"
 122: 
